Security: «remember me» cannot be made from the published file; what cut an order twice or held the queue [skip ci]

From the security review of the three programs (2026-11):
- «تذكرني»: the remembered sign-in could be written from the published permissions file alone (signing in as any
  user with no password). A password the admin makes with Admin 1.4 is published in a form that signs nobody in, and
  a remembered sign-in holds on its own computer only. A password not changed yet works as before.
- Every user on approved computers when the admin's permissions say so; the sign-in window shows this computer's code.
- An older permissions file put back, or the clock set back after a licence file was removed, is refused.
- The update's installer is downloaded to the program's own folder, not the shared Temp; the build's tools pinned.

From the independent review (each reproduced first, each with a test that fails on 2.0.18):
- orders of the same fabric nested in one marker, with two nestings at once: the order nested with another was given
  back to the queue before their marker was made and was cut a second time, alone — it stays taken now;
- a model that cannot be opened (held by another program) raised an error at every look and every model after it
  waited for ever — it is passed over for a minute, and named in the window after the third time;
- when LEVEL7 Nesting cannot work (nobody signed in on this computer, not found, the cutting folder away) every order
  of the queue was failed and moved to the errors folder — they wait now, the reason is shown, and the nesting goes on
  by itself;
- the pattern check looked at one piece of each NAME: pieces of several parts named alike («قطعة 1») are each checked;
- an error nobody foresaw while an order is made (its work folder cannot be made) left the line read and never made,
  with nothing said — «Needs attention», with the reason;
- two customers with orders of the same number in one folder: the second took the first one's waiting file for an
  older writing of itself and archived it — the second is held with the reason, the first untouched;
- LEVEL7 MTM opened twice on the same data read the orders and nested them twice — one at a time now;
- «Nest again» for an order of LEVEL7 and MTM said «not a readable GRAFIS file» — it is nested again;
- a licence file damaged, or a folder not writable for a moment, stopped the program with a traceback.

